    {
      "id": "claim_b1462ac761a6438d9fc5b3f3eb299c2f",
      "statement": "A stable external-contract selector should be authored on a plain React Native host node (a `View`/`Pressable` from `react-native`) with the Tamagui styling nested inside, because the failure mode of a `testID` that never reaches the DOM is a silent one — a `[data-testid=\"...\"]` locator matching zero elements times out rather than erroring. The reason is per-component prop plumbing rather than a blanket Tamagui limitation: Tamagui 3 does map `testID` to `data-testid` on its web path, so the design system's `Card` and `Banner` (and app-level `YStack` selectors such as `collection-card`) are targeted through `[data-testid=\"...\"]` in the web specs, while a component that drops or re-destructures the prop makes the attribute vanish. The host-node placement is what removes that variable. jest-expo renders React Native rather than React Native Web, so a `testID` on a Tamagui component passes the design-system unit tier and can still emit no `data-testid` on web; tests/e2e/web/settings.spec.ts's \"sub-navigation is locatable\" case is the discriminating check for host node versus Tamagui component.",
      "evidence": [
        {
