      "id": "claim_c5903eeb221b4fdf8a2b54c1570d4269",
      "statement": "The design system's `Card` and `Banner` place `testID` directly on a Tamagui node and their selectors are still resolved on web, which is why the host-node rule is a safe-placement convention rather than the only placement that works: `Card` spreads its remaining props onto the Tamagui `YStack` root, `Banner` passes `testID` to a Tamagui `View`, and web specs target the resulting `[data-testid]` values (`backup-schedule-editor`, `backup-error-banner`, and the app-level `collection-card` `YStack` selector).",
