    {
      "id": "claim_f87ac74dc5b84bf79687e1123cef9a00",
      "statement": "The design system's `Switch` is the standing example of the silent-drop failure and its fix: it used to destructure `...rest` without spreading it, so a passed `testID` reached nothing and a `[data-testid=\"...\"]` click timed out as if the screen were broken; it now spreads the remaining view props onto the `Pressable` that actually receives the press, and `controls.test.tsx` guards both that the id lands on the press target and that `accessibilityRole=\"switch\"` and the accessible name `getByRole` locators depend on survive the spread. `tests/e2e/web/admin-settings-access.spec.ts` asserts the same `testID` end to end on web.",
      "evidence": [
